<Base title="Copy review — Sondri">
  <section>
    <h1>Copy review</h1>
    <p>Round 1. Each entry reads: before → after → rule number or slop.</p>
    <p>Shared copy is included under each page that uses it. The workbench now keeps its copy locally. Rules and Copy review were added to the navigation.</p>
  </section>
  {pages.map((page) => (
    <section>
      <h2><a href={page.href}>{page.page}</a> · {page.entries.length} edits</h2>
      <ul>{page.entries.map(([before, after, rule]) => (
        <li><span>{before}</span> → <strong>{after}</strong> → <span>{rule === 'slop' ? 'slop' : `Rule ${rule}`}</span></li>
      ))}</ul>
    </section>
  ))}
  <section>
    <h2>Pattern check</h2>
    <p>No survivors for rules 2/5/12 search patterns. No three-short-sentence runs within a single copy block or heading variant.</p>
    <p>A flat text check joins separate heading variants on home-edgy: “Unsexy solutions that work ridiculously well. / Retire the fucking workaround. / Six things we build. Bring us the messy one.” and “Asked on almost every intro call. / Fine. Ask.” These are separate choices, not consecutive copy; each variant passes rule 6 on its own. The primary features heading remains flagged below.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Flagged, not changed</h2>
    <p>These five primary home-edgy headings are locked. All eleven primary headings remain byte-identical to the starting copy.</p>
    <ul>{flagged.map(([heading, rule]) => <li>{heading} → {rule}</li>)}</ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  li { margin-bottom: 16px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
